  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n- `app::lathe_voice::at_post` (the #1190 door) reads the script's dialect through main's `post::dialect::work_voice` (#1174) - no second parse of `capabilities`:\n  - `WorkSpindle` (mask has the turning bit): the door fires for every operation, as before.\n  - `ToolSpindle` (mask 1 alone): passes, as before.\n  - **`Undeclared`** (no mask naming 1 or 2: absent, 0, 4, a string, negative, non-finite): on a setup whose machine has a work spindle (lathe or mill-turn), the door refuses **every section except a C-axis live-tool section** (`voice_of` == `LiveTool`). That covers milling sections (a turning post would open them on the work spindle) *and* sections that turn the work (a turning kind, an on-centre Drill): only a turning post may post those (maintainer, 2026-11-12, #1232 / PR #1265), an unstated script is not known to be one, and a user's milling post without the line would post them as milling (tool change, `S M3`, the work standing still). The refusal says the script has no `capabilities` line and what to add (`capabilities = 1;` mill, `= 2;` turning), and for a turning section why. On a mill or with no machine an undeclared script passes, as before.\n- `at_post` takes the script's name for the refusal (`Option<&str>`): the per-mount post (`posting_mounts.rs`) and the per-op post (`posting_per_op.rs`) pass the setup post's registry name or path from `script_of`; the single-file `post_script` and an explicit script for all mounts pass `None` (\"the post script\").\n- `setup_workholding::work_speed`: the `(Undeclared, Some(_))` arm is unchanged; its stale comment now says what the door does.\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/1199-undeclared-dialect.md`: option (b) of the issue, with the stricter undeclared rule, a cell-by-cell table, the residual case (an undeclared *lathe* script on a mill / no-machine doc meets no door; not covered by #1265 either) and what was dropped.\n\nBehaviour change for users: a user's own script without `capabilities`, posting anything but a C-axis section on a lathe or mill-turn setup, is refused by name with the one-line fix. Every shipped post states its mask, so no shipped post, golden or registry pairing changes.\n\n## How tested\nPinning tests:\n- `camcraft-app` lib `lathe_voice::tests::an_undeclared_script_is_held_to_the_door_on_a_machine_with_a_work_spindle`: undeclared scripts (none, `\"2\"`, `-1`, `0`, `4`) on a lathe and a mill-turn refuse Face, off-centre Drill, Facing and on-centre Drill by name (missing line, machine, both fixes; turning sections say only a turning post may post them), pass a C-stating live-tool section, and name the script when given; declared `1` / `2` on the same machines behave as stated; on a mill and with no machine everything passes.\n- `crates/app/tests/lathe_workholding_mill_post.rs` `every_machine_dialect_and_section_cell_gives_its_verdict`: the `undeclared` row is \"not judged\" on lathe / mill-turn for both sections (the door refuses first), and those cells assert the door's text.\n- Unchanged and green: `lathe_voice::tests::the_door_refuses_on_every_turning_dialect_and_passes_every_milling_one`, `post::dialect` tests (main's), `lathe_workholding_kinds::an_undeclared_script_takes_the_stricter_reading` (mill machine, unchanged).\n\nGate on head `27dee0df` (macOS, debug, all green): camcraft-app lib (147), camcraft-post lib (38); app suites `lathe_workholding_mill_post`, `lathe_work_spindle`, `lathe_workholding_kinds`, `lathe_workholding_live`, `posting`, `lathe_post_refusals`, `lathe_post`, `per_op_files`, `setup_mounts_post`, `conformance`, `golden_cl`, plus every other suite that posts on a lathe / mill-turn machine or touches the post door: `lathe_workholding_rpm`, `lathe_post_g76`, `drill_prior`, `lathe_cross_drill`, `c_axis_live`, `mcp_live`, `setup_post_options`, `post_not_judged`; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Merges cleanly with upstream main (not merged in).\n\n## Not exercised\n- The GUI/MCP post entry points end-to-end with a user `.cps` file on disk (they all reach `at_post` through the three post bodies).\n- The rest of the app suites (batch tier).\n\nChangelog: A post script that does not state `capabilities` posts only C-axis live-tool sections on a lathe or mill-turn setup; every other section (milling or turning) is refused by name with the manifest line to add, instead of being read as a mill post (#1199)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1199\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
